window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity-results":{"contents":"* Connected.card_connectedComponent: a connected graph has exactly one connected\n  component.* hypercube_connected: the n-dimensional hypercube is connected.* connected_mycielskian_iff: the Mycielskian mμ[G] is connected iff G has no\n  isolated vertices.* isBridge_mycielskian_iff: the bridges of mμ[G] are the edges none — u ᵣ with\n  u isolated in G.* pathNat₁_connected / pathNat₁_isAcyclic / pathNat₁_isTree: the infinite path\n  on ℕ is a tree (so every edge is a bridge).* Walk.exists_odd_isCycle / isBipartite_iff_forall_isCycle_even: a closed walk of\n  odd length contains a cycle of odd length, so a graph is bipartite iff it has no\n  odd cycle.* Walk.IsCycle.mem_support_of_degree_le_two /\n  Walk.IsCycle.isHamiltonianCycle_of_degree_le_two: in a graph of maximum degree at\n  most 2, every cycle passes through every vertex of its component, so in a\n  connected such graph every cycle is a Hamiltonian cycle.* Walk.exists_isEulerian_circuit: Euler's Theorem, existence direction (if all\n  edges lie in one component and every vertex has even degree, there is an Eulerian\n  circuit).* Walk.exists_isEulerian_trail_of_two_odd: if all edges lie in one component and\n  exactly two vertices a ≠ b have odd degree, there is an Eulerian trail from a\n  to b.* hypercube_isEdgeConnected: the n-dimensional hypercube is n-edge-connected.* hypercube_isVertexConnected: the n-dimensional hypercube is\n  n-vertex-connected.* isVertexConnected_iff_induce: G is k-vertex-connected iff it has more than\n  k vertices and G.induce Sᶜ is preconnected whenever S.encard < k.* vertexConnectivity_le_edgeConnectivity: κ(G) ≤ λ(G) for every\n  graph.* brooks_two: Brooks' theorem for Δ = 2, a finite graph of maximum degree at\n  most 2 is 2-colourable unless one of its components is an odd cycle.* brooks: Brooks' theorem for Δ ≥ 3, a finite graph with maximum degree\n  at most Δ and no (Δ + 1)-clique is Δ-colourable.* colorable_of_cliqueFree_of_degree_le: the same for locally finite graphs.* brooks_general: Brooks' theorem for every Δ.* isVertexConnected_two_iff: a graph is 2-vertex-connected iff it has at least\n  three vertices, is connected and has no cut vertex.* IsCutVertex.splitsAt / splitsAt_of_not_reachable: a graph splits at each of its\n  cut vertices, and at every vertex if its edges lie in two different components.* colorable_of_forall_block: for n ≥ 1, a finite graph is n-colourable if\n  each of its blocks is.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* IsTree.degree_le_card_leaves: a finite tree has at least as many leaves as the\n  degree of any of its vertices.* Walk.exists_odd_isCycle_length_le: a closed walk of odd length k contains an\n  odd cycle of length at most k.* IsVertexConnected.le_minDegree: a k-vertex-connected graph has minimum degree\n  at least k.* edgeConnectivity_le_minDegree: λ(G) ≤ δ(G) for a finite graph\n  with at least two vertices (completing Whitney's inequalities).* hypercube_vertexConnectivity / hypercube_edgeConnectivity: κ(Q[n]) = n,\n  and λ(Q[n + 1]) = n + 1 (while λ(Q[0]) = ⊤).* IsAcyclic.blockOf_eq: in a forest the block of an edge is that single edge.* colorable_iff_forall_block: for n ≥ 1, a graph is n-colourable iff each of\n  its blocks is.\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Results","header":"14.3.8. Chapter 10: Connectivity (Results)","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity-results"}});